/! The outcome
section#outcome
	.container
		.row.justify-content-between.g-5
			.col-12.col-md-5.position-sticky.d-flex.align-items-center.vh-100.mx-auto.top-0
				.flex-grow-1
					h2 The outcome
					p.lead.mb-4 The finished website gave the client a dedicated digital presence that is clean, engaging, and easy to navigate. It provides students and other stakeholders with a clear, accessible entry point into career training, resources, and support while better communicating the initiative’s mission and programs.
					p.lead The final experience also brought the visual identity established during the design process to life across the website. Typography, bespoke graphic elements, and consistent interface styles created a more cohesive digital presence while building on the client’s existing logo.
					p.lead For development, I translated the approved designs into a custom WordPress Gutenberg theme with reusable custom blocks. This maintained consistency with the original mockups while giving the client greater flexibility to manage content and expand the website as their needs evolve.
					/ h6
					/ 	span.badge.text-bg-secondary Problem
					/ p A youth career initiative in Baltimore needed a standalone digital presence. Previously limited to a single landing page within another organization’s website, they required a dedicated microsite that reflected their brand, shared their story, and guided students toward training opportunities and career resources.
					/ h6
					/ 	span.badge.text-bg-secondary Process
					/ p Drio Duo partnered with me to design and develop the new website. I created high-fidelity mockups based on their updated brand and messaging, then built a responsive WordPress site focused on simplicity, accessibility, and clear resource pathways for students, educators, and community partners.
					/ h6
					/ 	span.badge.text-bg-secondary Outcome
					/ p The finished microsite is clean, engaging, and easy to navigate, providing students and stakeholders with a clear, accessible entry point into career training, resources, and support.

